ize-small"><svg data-v-351fdc4e="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify simple-button-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-351fdc4e="">Copy</span></div> <div data-v-351fdc4e="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="simple-button size-small"><svg data-v-351fdc4e="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify simple-button-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Share_a"><path d="M386.218667 247.850667c0-102.4 120.405333-157.397333 197.76-90.282667l304.426666 264.32a119.466667 119.466667 0 0 1 1.365334 179.285333l-304.469334 272.170667c-76.970667 68.778667-199.082667 14.122667-199.082666-89.088v-89.173333c-33.024 2.261333-59.306667 6.826667-83.2 15.36-30.592 10.88-61.866667 29.952-98.602667 67.712a76.8 76.8 0 0 1-131.84-53.504c0-98.645333 24.106667-190.976 83.712-261.888 55.253333-65.792 133.973333-104.789333 229.930667-117.845334V247.850667z m147.413333-32.256c-27.648-23.978667-70.613333-4.352-70.613333 32.256v126.208l-0.256 4.309333c-2.218667 21.504-20.437333 38.186667-42.410667 40.021333l-17.194667 1.706667c-173.994667 20.949333-253.824 136.405333-253.824 304.554667 86.997333-89.557333 163.925333-105.386667 270.933334-107.861334a42.026667 42.026667 0 0 1 42.752 42.24v125.226667c0 34.56 38.272 53.845333 65.706666 35.925333l5.376-4.096 304.426667-272.213333a42.666667 42.666667 0 0 0 2.986667-60.714667l-3.413334-3.285333-304.469333-264.277333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-351fdc4e="">Share</span></div> <!----></div> <!----></div>   <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div></div></div></div><div data-v-38e35b58="" class="chat-content-item chat-content-item-assistant" data-archer-id="19f249f2-8172-8e1b-8000-0a166e53ee4d"><!----> <div data-v-a660adc4="" data-v-38e35b58="" class="segment segment-assistant"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-avatar"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" class="avatar"><canvas data-v-b81624a4="" data-v-88be9e2e="" style="width: 56px; height: 56px;" class="rive-container" width="112" height="112"></canvas></div></div> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-container" dir="auto"> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content"><div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content-box"> <!----> <div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user says they got a "No such file" error. This is likely from trying to mount <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev/sda1</code> to <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/mnt/parrot/boot/efi</code>. The issue is that <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/mnt/parrot/boot/efi</code> directory might not exist, or <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev/sda1</code> might not be the correct EFI partition.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me think about this:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">From the fdisk output earlier, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev/sda1</code> was 100MB EFI System partition</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But maybe the directory <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/mnt/parrot/boot/efi</code> doesn't exist in the mounted Parrot filesystem</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I should ask them to:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Check if <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/mnt/parrot/boot/efi</code> exists</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">If not, create it</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Then try mounting again</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or alternatively, the EFI partition might be on a different device. Let me also consider that maybe <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev/sda1</code> is not the right partition - but from fdisk it showed as 100MB EFI System.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, looking back at the fdisk output from earlier screenshots:</div><ul start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev/sda1</code> - 100MB EFI System</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev/sda2</code> - 16M Microsoft reserved</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev/sda3</code> - 160.4G Microsoft basic data</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev/sda4</code> - 52.2G Linux filesystem (Parrot)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev/sda5</code> - 7.8G Microsoft basic data</div></li></ul><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">So <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev/sda1</code> should be the EFI partition. The "No such file" error is likely because <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/mnt/parrot/boot/efi</code> directory doesn't exist. I need to create it first.</div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!----> <!----> <!----> <!---->   <!----> <div data-v-38e35b58="" class="okc-cards-container"><!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div> <!----> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-b1bd13bb="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-assistant-actions"><div data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="segment-assistant-actions-content"> <!----> <!----> <!----><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <!----></div><!----> <!----><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/