height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-351fdc4e="">Copy</span></div> <div data-v-351fdc4e="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="simple-button size-small"><svg data-v-351fdc4e="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify simple-button-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Share_a"><path d="M386.218667 247.850667c0-102.4 120.405333-157.397333 197.76-90.282667l304.426666 264.32a119.466667 119.466667 0 0 1 1.365334 179.285333l-304.469334 272.170667c-76.970667 68.778667-199.082667 14.122667-199.082666-89.088v-89.173333c-33.024 2.261333-59.306667 6.826667-83.2 15.36-30.592 10.88-61.866667 29.952-98.602667 67.712a76.8 76.8 0 0 1-131.84-53.504c0-98.645333 24.106667-190.976 83.712-261.888 55.253333-65.792 133.973333-104.789333 229.930667-117.845334V247.850667z m147.413333-32.256c-27.648-23.978667-70.613333-4.352-70.613333 32.256v126.208l-0.256 4.309333c-2.218667 21.504-20.437333 38.186667-42.410667 40.021333l-17.194667 1.706667c-173.994667 20.949333-253.824 136.405333-253.824 304.554667 86.997333-89.557333 163.925333-105.386667 270.933334-107.861334a42.026667 42.026667 0 0 1 42.752 42.24v125.226667c0 34.56 38.272 53.845333 65.706666 35.925333l5.376-4.096 304.426667-272.213333a42.666667 42.666667 0 0 0 2.986667-60.714667l-3.413334-3.285333-304.469333-264.277333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-351fdc4e="">Share</span></div> <!----></div> <!----></div>   <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div></div></div></div><div data-v-38e35b58="" class="chat-content-item chat-content-item-assistant" data-archer-id="19f24b51-46a2-8f6b-8000-0a16fae9de0b"><!----> <div data-v-a660adc4="" data-v-38e35b58="" class="segment segment-assistant"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-avatar"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" class="avatar"><canvas data-v-b81624a4="" data-v-88be9e2e="" style="width: 56px; height: 56px;" class="rive-container" width="112" height="112"></canvas></div></div> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-container" dir="auto"> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content"><div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content-box"> <!----> <div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Same error means <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> still isn't properly available inside chroot. Let me think about this differently.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The issue is that <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --bind /dev /mnt/parrot/dev</code> might be binding SystemRescue's broken <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> (which lacks proper device nodes due to the missing proc/sys files).</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me try a different approach: use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mknod</code> to create the essential device files, or use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --rbind</code> instead of <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--bind</code>, or mount <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> as a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">devtmpfs</code>.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, the best approach for SystemRescue is to use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --rbind</code> (recursive bind) which includes all sub-mounts, or to mount a fresh <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">devtmpfs</code>.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me give the user the alternative approaches:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --rbind /dev /mnt/parrot/dev</code> - recursive bind</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount -t devtmpfs devtmpfs /mnt/parrot/dev</code> - fresh devtmpfs</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Skip chroot entirely and run grub-install with <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--boot-directory</code> flag from outside</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, option 3 might be the simplest fix. Let me try that.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Wait, but the user already tried <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grub-install --boot-directory=/mnt/parrot/boot /dev/sda</code> earlier in the context and it didn't work well. But that was before we had the EFI partition properly set up.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me think again. The problem is that inside chroot, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> doesn't have the proper device files. This is because SystemRescue's <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> might be a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">devtmpfs</code> that doesn't bind properly.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me try:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --rbind /dev /mnt/parrot/dev</code> instead of <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--bind</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or mount devtmpfs directly: <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount -t devtmpfs devtmpfs /mnt/parrot/dev</code></div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, let me also consider: maybe we need to mount <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/sys</code> as well for GRUB to detect devices properly. Even though I said it's optional, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grub-install</code> might need it to enumerate devices.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me give the user a comprehensive fix:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token comment"># Exit chroot first</span>
<span class="token builtin class-name">exit</span>

<span class="token comment"># Unmount the broken dev bind</span>
<span class="token function">umount</span> /mnt/parrot/dev

<span class="token comment"># Use recursive bind or devtmpfs</span>
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">--rbind</span> /dev /mnt/parrot/dev
<span class="token function">mount</span> --make-rslave /mnt/parrot/dev

<span class="token comment"># Also mount sys properly</span>
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> sysfs sysfs /mnt/parrot/sys

<span class="token comment"># Then chroot again</span>
<span class="token function">chroot</span> /mnt/parrot
grub-install /dev/sda</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or alternatively, skip chroot and use the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--boot-directory</code> approach with the EFI directory properly mounted:</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually wait - looking at the error again: "cannot find a device for /boot/grub (is /dev mounted?)". This is specifically about <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> not having device nodes.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The cleanest fix might be to use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --rbind</code> or to create a devtmpfs. Let me provide both options.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, I just realized something. The user said "Same error" - they ran <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">chroot /mnt/parrot</code> then <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grub-install /dev/sda</code> and got the same error. But they didn't show me the screenshot. Let me just give them the fix.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The most reliable fix for SystemRescue is:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token builtin class-name">exit</span>
<span class="token function">umount</span> /mnt/parrot/dev
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">--rbind</span> /dev /mnt/parrot/dev
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">--rbind</span> /sys /mnt/parrot/sys
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">--rbind</span> /proc /mnt/parrot/proc
<span class="token function">chroot</span> /mnt/parrot
grub-install /dev/sda</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or even simpler - use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount -t devtmpfs</code>:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token builtin class-name">exit</span>
<span class="token function">umount</span> /mnt/parrot/dev
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> devtmpfs devtmpfs /mnt/parrot/dev
<span class="token function">chroot</span> /mnt/parrot
grub-install /dev/sda</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me give them the devtmpfs approach first as it's the cleanest. If that doesn't work, we'll try rbind.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, let me reconsider. The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--rbind</code> approach is probably better because it preserves all the device files and special files from the host. Let me provide that.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Wait, I also need to think about whether <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/sys</code> is needed. The error specifically says "is /dev mounted?" so it's about <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code>. But GRUB might also need <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/sys</code> to detect the boot device. Let me include both.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Here's my plan:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Exit chroot</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Unmount the broken <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> bind</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--rbind</code> for <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/sys</code>, <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/proc</code></div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Chroot again</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Run grub-install</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me give this to the user concisely. Same error means <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> still isn't working inside chroot. Let's fix it properly.</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token builtin class-name">exit</span>
<span class="token function">umount</span> /mnt/parrot/dev
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">--rbind</span> /dev /mnt/parrot/dev
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">--rbind</span> /sys /mnt/parrot/sys
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">--rbind</span> /proc /mnt/parrot/proc
<span class="token function">chroot</span> /mnt/parrot
grub-install /dev/sda</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Run <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">exit</code> first, then these commands one by one.</strong></div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!----> <!----> <!----> <!---->   <!----> <div data-v-38e35b58="" class="okc-cards-container"><!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div> <!----> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-b1bd13bb="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-assistant-actions"><div data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="segment-assistant-actions-content"> <!----> <!----> <!----><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <!----></div><!----> <!----><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024