ple-button-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-351fdc4e="">Copy</span></div> <div data-v-351fdc4e="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="simple-button size-small"><svg data-v-351fdc4e="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify simple-button-icon" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Share_a"><path d="M386.218667 247.850667c0-102.4 120.405333-157.397333 197.76-90.282667l304.426666 264.32a119.466667 119.466667 0 0 1 1.365334 179.285333l-304.469334 272.170667c-76.970667 68.778667-199.082667 14.122667-199.082666-89.088v-89.173333c-33.024 2.261333-59.306667 6.826667-83.2 15.36-30.592 10.88-61.866667 29.952-98.602667 67.712a76.8 76.8 0 0 1-131.84-53.504c0-98.645333 24.106667-190.976 83.712-261.888 55.253333-65.792 133.973333-104.789333 229.930667-117.845334V247.850667z m147.413333-32.256c-27.648-23.978667-70.613333-4.352-70.613333 32.256v126.208l-0.256 4.309333c-2.218667 21.504-20.437333 38.186667-42.410667 40.021333l-17.194667 1.706667c-173.994667 20.949333-253.824 136.405333-253.824 304.554667 86.997333-89.557333 163.925333-105.386667 270.933334-107.861334a42.026667 42.026667 0 0 1 42.752 42.24v125.226667c0 34.56 38.272 53.845333 65.706666 35.925333l5.376-4.096 304.426667-272.213333a42.666667 42.666667 0 0 0 2.986667-60.714667l-3.413334-3.285333-304.469333-264.277333z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <span data-v-351fdc4e="">Share</span></div> <!----></div> <!----></div>   <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div></div></div></div><div data-v-38e35b58="" class="chat-content-item chat-content-item-assistant" data-archer-id="19f24be5-0912-8679-8000-0a16dc3de88d"><!----> <div data-v-a660adc4="" data-v-38e35b58="" class="segment segment-assistant"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-avatar"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" class="avatar"><canvas data-v-b81624a4="" data-v-88be9e2e="" style="width: 56px; height: 56px;" class="rive-container" width="112" height="112"></canvas></div></div> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-container" dir="auto"> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content"><div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content-box"> <!----> <div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">I can see the issue now. Looking at the screenshot:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">umount /mnt/parrot/dev</code> failed with <strong>"target is busy"</strong> — the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> bind mount is stuck and can't be unmounted.</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user also tried <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --rbind /dev /mnt/parrot/dev</code> and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --make-rslave /mnt/parrot/dev</code> and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount -t sysfs sysfs /mnt/parrot/sys</code>, but the chroot still failed with the same error.</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The fundamental problem is that SystemRescue's <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> is broken (missing <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id</code> and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/proc/sys/kernel/random/uuid</code>), and binding it into the chroot doesn't help because the device files inside SystemRescue's <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> are also incomplete.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>New approach: Skip chroot entirely and run <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grub-install</code> from outside with the correct paths.</strong></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me give the user a completely different strategy:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token comment"># From OUTSIDE chroot (you're already outside)</span>
<span class="token comment"># Install GRUB directly to the disk, pointing to the mounted Parrot filesystem</span>
grub-install --boot-directory<span class="token operator">=</span>/mnt/parrot/boot --efi-directory<span class="token operator">=</span>/mnt/parrot/boot/efi <span class="token parameter variable">--target</span><span class="token operator">=</span>x86_64-efi <span class="token parameter variable">--removable</span> /dev/sda</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Wait, but this uses SystemRescue's grub-install which might not work with Parrot's GRUB configuration.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, let me think about this more carefully. The error inside chroot is "cannot find a device for /boot/grub (is /dev mounted?)". This means GRUB inside chroot can't find the block device corresponding to <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/boot/grub</code>.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The issue is that <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> inside the chroot doesn't have proper block device nodes. SystemRescue uses a minimal <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> that doesn't include all the standard Linux device files.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Alternative approach: Use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mknod</code> to create the essential device files inside the chroot, or use <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">devtmpfs</code>.</strong></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, the cleanest solution might be:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token comment"># Force unmount the busy dev</span>
<span class="token function">umount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-l</span> /mnt/parrot/dev

<span class="token comment"># Mount a fresh devtmpfs</span>
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> devtmpfs devtmpfs /mnt/parrot/dev

<span class="token comment"># Also mount proc and sys properly</span>
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> proc proc /mnt/parrot/proc
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> sysfs sysfs /mnt/parrot/sys

<span class="token comment"># Then chroot</span>
<span class="token function">chroot</span> /mnt/parrot
grub-install /dev/sda</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But wait, the user already tried <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount -t sysfs sysfs /mnt/parrot/sys</code> and it seemed to work (no error shown). The issue is specifically with <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code>.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me try the devtmpfs approach. But first, let me force unmount the busy <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code>:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token function">umount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-l</span> /mnt/parrot/dev
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> devtmpfs devtmpfs /mnt/parrot/dev</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Or even simpler - let me try running grub-install WITHOUT chroot, using SystemRescue's own grub-install but pointing to the Parrot boot directory:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash">grub-install --boot-directory<span class="token operator">=</span>/mnt/parrot/boot --efi-directory<span class="token operator">=</span>/mnt/parrot/boot/efi <span class="token parameter variable">--target</span><span class="token operator">=</span>x86_64-efi /dev/sda</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But this might not work because SystemRescue's GRUB might not be compatible with Parrot's.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, the BEST approach is to fix the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> inside chroot. Let me try:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token comment"># Force lazy unmount</span>
<span class="token function">umount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-l</span> /mnt/parrot/dev

<span class="token comment"># Create essential device nodes manually</span>
<span class="token function">mknod</span> /mnt/parrot/dev/null c <span class="token number">1</span> <span class="token number">3</span>
<span class="token function">mknod</span> /mnt/parrot/dev/zero c <span class="token number">1</span> <span class="token number">5</span>
<span class="token function">mknod</span> /mnt/parrot/dev/random c <span class="token number">1</span> <span class="token number">8</span>
<span class="token function">mknod</span> /mnt/parrot/dev/urandom c <span class="token number">1</span> <span class="token number">9</span>
<span class="token function">mknod</span> /mnt/parrot/dev/tty c <span class="token number">5</span> <span class="token number">0</span>
<span class="token function">mknod</span> /mnt/parrot/dev/sda b <span class="token number">8</span> <span class="token number">0</span>
<span class="token function">mknod</span> /mnt/parrot/dev/sda1 b <span class="token number">8</span> <span class="token number">1</span>
<span class="token function">mknod</span> /mnt/parrot/dev/sda2 b <span class="token number">8</span> <span class="token number">2</span>
<span class="token function">mknod</span> /mnt/parrot/dev/sda3 b <span class="token number">8</span> <span class="token number">3</span>
<span class="token function">mknod</span> /mnt/parrot/dev/sda4 b <span class="token number">8</span> <span class="token number">4</span>
<span class="token function">mknod</span> /mnt/parrot/dev/sda5 b <span class="token number">8</span> <span class="token number">5</span></code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But this is tedious and error-prone.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, let me try a simpler approach. The issue might be that we need to mount <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> as a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">devtmpfs</code> filesystem, not a bind mount. SystemRescue's <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> is a <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">devtmpfs</code>, and when we bind-mount it, the device nodes don't transfer properly because they're dynamically created by the kernel.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me try:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token function">umount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-l</span> /mnt/parrot/dev
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> devtmpfs devtmpfs /mnt/parrot/dev</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">This should create a fresh devtmpfs with all the proper device nodes.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Wait, actually I just realized something. The user ran <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --rbind /dev /mnt/parrot/dev</code> and then <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --make-rslave /mnt/parrot/dev</code>. The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--rbind</code> should have worked better than <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--bind</code> because it includes all sub-mounts. But the chroot still failed.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me look at this from a different angle. Maybe the issue isn't with <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> at all, but with how GRUB is trying to find the device. The error says "cannot find a device for /boot/grub". This might mean GRUB can't determine which physical device <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/boot/grub</code> is on.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">This could be because:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/proc</code> isn't properly mounted (so GRUB can't read <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/proc/mounts</code> or <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/proc/self/mountinfo</code>)</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/sys</code> isn't properly mounted (so GRUB can't use sysfs to find block devices)</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The user did mount <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/proc</code> with <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--bind</code>, but SystemRescue's <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/proc</code> might also be broken (as evidenced by the missing <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id</code>).</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me try mounting a fresh <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">proc</code> filesystem:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token function">umount</span> /mnt/parrot/proc
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> proc proc /mnt/parrot/proc</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">And also ensure <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/sys</code> is mounted:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> sysfs sysfs /mnt/parrot/sys</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Then try chroot again.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, I think the real issue is simpler. Let me look at what the user actually ran:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --rbind /dev /mnt/parrot/dev</code> - this should work</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --make-rslave /mnt/parrot/dev</code> - this is for unmount propagation, not needed here</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount -t sysfs sysfs /mnt/parrot/sys</code> - this worked</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">chroot /mnt/parrot</code> - worked</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">grub-install /dev/sda</code> - FAILED with same error</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">So even with <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--rbind</code> for <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> and <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">sysfs</code> for <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/sys</code>, it still fails. This suggests the problem is deeper.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Wait, I just noticed something. The user ran <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">mount --rbind /dev /mnt/parrot/dev</code> but the original <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--bind</code> mount of <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> was still there from earlier. So now there might be TWO mounts on <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/mnt/parrot/dev</code> - the old <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--bind</code> and the new <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--rbind</code>. That could cause issues.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Also, the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">umount /mnt/parrot/dev</code> failed with "target is busy" because the chroot was still active when they tried to unmount. They exited chroot, but maybe some process was still holding the mount.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">OK let me think about this differently. The simplest and most reliable approach is:</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Approach 1: Use SystemRescue's grub-install directly without chroot</strong></div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash">grub-install --boot-directory<span class="token operator">=</span>/mnt/parrot/boot --efi-directory<span class="token operator">=</span>/mnt/parrot/boot/efi <span class="token parameter variable">--target</span><span class="token operator">=</span>x86_64-efi <span class="token parameter variable">--removable</span> /dev/sda</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But SystemRescue might not have the Parrot GRUB modules.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Approach 2: Fix the chroot environment properly</strong></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">The key insight: we need ALL virtual filesystems to be fresh mounts, not bind mounts from the broken SystemRescue environment.</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token comment"># Unmount everything from parrot</span>
<span class="token function">umount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-R</span> /mnt/parrot

<span class="token comment"># Remount root</span>
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-o</span> <span class="token assign-left variable">subvol</span><span class="token operator">=</span>@ /dev/sda4 /mnt/parrot

<span class="token comment"># Mount fresh virtual filesystems</span>
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> devtmpfs devtmpfs /mnt/parrot/dev
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> proc proc /mnt/parrot/proc
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> sysfs sysfs /mnt/parrot/sys
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> tmpfs tmpfs /mnt/parrot/run

<span class="token comment"># Chroot and install</span>
<span class="token function">chroot</span> /mnt/parrot
grub-install /dev/sda
<span class="token function">update-grub</span></code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">This approach uses FRESH mounts for all virtual filesystems instead of binding SystemRescue's broken ones.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Approach 3: Use the <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">--boot-directory</code> flag with the chrooted grub-install</strong></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually wait, there's another option. The error says "cannot find a device for /boot/grub". Maybe we need to specify the boot directory explicitly:</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token function">chroot</span> /mnt/parrot
grub-install --boot-directory<span class="token operator">=</span>/boot /dev/sda</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">But <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/boot</code> is the default, so this shouldn't make a difference.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me go with <strong>Approach 2</strong> - the fresh mount approach. This is the most reliable because it avoids all the broken bind mounts from SystemRescue.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Actually, I want to be even more careful. Let me also consider: maybe the issue is that <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> inside SystemRescue doesn't have the block device nodes for <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev/sda</code> because it's a minimal environment. Let me check what <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">ls /dev/sd*</code> shows in SystemRescue.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">From the earlier <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">lsblk</code> output, we know <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">sda</code> exists. So the device nodes should be there.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Hmm, but the bind mount of <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> into the chroot might not include the block device major/minor numbers properly if SystemRescue's <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> is using a special filesystem.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">OK, I'm overcomplicating this. Let me just give the user the cleanest approach:</div><ol start="1"><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Unmount everything</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Remount root</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Use fresh devtmpfs, proc, sysfs mounts</div></li><li><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Chroot and install</div></li></ol><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Let me write this clearly. The <code data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code-inline">/dev</code> bind mount is stuck ("target is busy"). Let's start fresh.</div><div data-v-8d822fd1="" data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="segment-code"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="sticky-release" style="--sticky-header-height: 42.5px;"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-rail"><div data-v-13fde6a9="" class="sticky-release-header" style="top: 0px;"><header data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header"><div data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-header-content"><span data-v-8d822fd1="" class="segment-code-lang">bash</span> <!----> <span data-v-868ea423="" data-v-8d822fd1=""><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-868ea423="" class="icon-button" style="width: 32px; height: 32px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <div data-v-5f9e9bf6="" data-v-1005b780="" class="kimi-tooltip tooltip-bottom icon-button-tooltip bottom">Copy</div></div></span></div></header></div></div></div> <div data-v-efb858b9="" data-v-8d822fd1="" class="syntax-highlighter dark segment-code-content"><pre data-v-efb858b9="" class="language-bash"><code class="language-bash"><span class="token function">umount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-R</span> /mnt/parrot
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-o</span> <span class="token assign-left variable">subvol</span><span class="token operator">=</span>@ /dev/sda4 /mnt/parrot
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> devtmpfs devtmpfs /mnt/parrot/dev
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> proc proc /mnt/parrot/proc
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> sysfs sysfs /mnt/parrot/sys
<span class="token function">mount</span> <span class="token parameter variable">-t</span> tmpfs tmpfs /mnt/parrot/run
<span class="token function">chroot</span> /mnt/parrot
grub-install /dev/sda</code></pre></div></div> <div data-v-d664c8c3=""></div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Run this now.</strong></div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!----> <!----> <!----> <!---->   <!----> <div data-v-38e35b58="" class="okc-cards-container"><!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div> <!----> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-b1bd13bb="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-assistant-actions"><div data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="segment-assistant-actions-content"> <!----> <!----> <!----><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 40.106667 89.6 89.6 89.6h256a89.6 89.6 0 0 0 89.6-89.6v-256A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 725.333333 379.733333h-256z" fill="currentColor"></path><path d="M554.666667 132.266667a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 144.128 83.2 38.4 38.4 0 0 1-66.517334 38.4A89.514667 89.514667 0 0 0 554.666667 209.066667H298.666667A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 209.066667 298.666667v256c0 33.109333 17.92 62.08 44.8 77.653333a38.4 38.4 0 0 1-38.4 66.474667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 132.266667 554.666667V298.666667A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 298.666667 132.266667h256z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg> <!----></div><!----> <!----><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Refresh"><path d="M303.104 315.392c114.688-114.688 303.104-114.688 417.792 0l-32.768 32.768c-20.48 2