v-38e35b58="" class="segment segment-assistant"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-avatar"><div data-v-88be9e2e="" class="avatar"><canvas data-v-b81624a4="" data-v-88be9e2e="" style="width: 56px; height: 56px;" class="rive-container" width="112" height="112"></canvas></div></div> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-container" dir="auto"> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content"><div data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-content-box"> <!----> <div data-v-3b9ae98b="" data-v-d664c8c3="" class="markdown-container"><div data-v-3b9ae98b="" class="markdown"><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">Yes, exactly! The blinking cursor might mean the system is stuck trying to boot.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto"><strong>Press and hold the power button for 5-10 seconds</strong> to force shutdown, then <strong>press the power button again</strong> to turn it back on.</div><div class="paragraph" dir="auto">It should boot from the hard disk and show the GRUB menu with your Parrot OS and Windows options. Let me know what you see! 🚀</div></div></div> <!----> <!----> <!----></div>  <!----> <!----> <!----> <!---->   <!----> <div data-v-38e35b58="" class="okc-cards-container"><!----> <!----> <!----> <!----> <!----></div> <!----> <!----> <!----> <div data-v-b1bd13bb="" data-v-a660adc4="" class="segment-assistant-actions"><div data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="segment-assistant-actions-content"> <!----> <!----> <!----><div data-v-1005b780="" data-v-b1bd13bb="" class="icon-button" style="width: 28px; height: 28px;"><svg data-v-1005b780="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" role="img" class="iconify" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 1024 1024" name="Copy"><path d="M725.333333 302.933333a166.4 166.4 0 0 1 166.4 166.4v256a166.4 166.4 0 0 1-166.4 166.4h-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 302.933333 725.333333v-256A166.4 166.4 0 0 1 469.333333 302.933333h256z m-256 76.8A89.6 89.6 0 0 0 379.733333 469.333333v256c0 49.493333 4